            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0321" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-16T13:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>117. All quiet. Situation much improved. Policing in Port-au-Prince and Cape
                    Haitien in entire charge of garde with exception of one patrol at
                    Port-au-Prince. Restriction on circulation at night will be entirely removed
                    today. Students Damien Medical School and Law School still on strike.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
